   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Indirect questions",
     "texto": [
      "To say «whether…» inside a sentence, use **-는지** with verbs in the present (**오는지** = whether (he/she) comes), **-았/었는지** in the past (**왔는지** = whether (he/she) came) and **-(으)ㄹ지** for something in the future or uncertain (**올지** = whether (he/she) will come). With adjectives: **-(으)ㄴ지** in the present (**좋은지**) and **-았/었는지** in the past (**좋았는지**); with nouns, **-(이)ㄴ지** (**학생인지**).",
      "이 답이 **맞는지** 모르겠어요 = I don't know whether this answer is correct."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Presenting alternatives",
     "texto": [
      "To ask whether one option or the other is met, the forms can be repeated: 가는지 안 가는지 = whether (he/she) goes or not; 큰지 작은지 = whether it is big or small. The full sentence usually takes a verb such as **알다, 모르다, 묻다** or **궁금하다**.",
      "With verbs of speaking, **-는지** expresses an indirect question; it is not the marker for quoting a statement word for word."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
